<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 42-day T-bills 64 pct sold, yield 39 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 42-day T-bills 64 pct sold, yield 39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 3.0 billion levs of 42-day floater coupon T-bills was 63.8-percent sold, yielding 39.20 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry for Friday's auction.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 300 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG 3019196024</p>
<p> Par value			 3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		    October 11, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			October 17, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		   November 28, 1996</p>
<p> Bids received		   1,973.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	     96.46 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		   1,913.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	    96.64 levs</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   39.20 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
